1
00:00:02,001 --> 00:00:04,796
A SHORT TIME AGO IN AN APARTMENT
IN PASADENA....

2
00:00:17,475 --> 00:00:22,647
THE OPENING NIGHT EXCITATION

3
00:00:22,730 --> 00:00:25,108
IT IS A PERIOD OF GREAT TENSION.

4
00:00:25,192 --> 00:00:27,652
OUR HEROES, LEONARD, SHELDON,
WOLOWITZ AND KOOTHRAPPALI

5
00:00:27,735 --> 00:00:30,113
KNOW THAT TICKETS
TO THE NEW STAR WARS MOVIE

6
00:00:30,197 --> 00:00:33,491
ARE ABOUT TO BE AVAILABLE FOR PRE-SALE.

7
00:00:33,575 --> 00:00:37,579
IF THEY FAIL IN THEIR MISSION
AND CAN'T SEE IT ON OPENING NIGHT

8
00:00:37,662 --> 00:00:40,248
SHELDON HAS SWORN THAT
THEY WILL NEVER HEAR THE END OF IT

9
00:00:40,332 --> 00:00:42,959
FOR THE REST OF THEIR LIVES...

10
00:00:43,042 --> 00:00:46,463
THEY BELIEVE HIM.

11
00:00:57,640 --> 00:00:59,684
-Guys, tickets already went on sale!
-What?

12
00:00:59,851 --> 00:01:01,311
They're not supposed to be available yet.

13
00:01:01,478 --> 00:01:02,979
I don't know what to tell you,
but they're on sale!

14
00:01:03,480 --> 00:01:05,607
(STAMMERS) Wait. Are you sure
they're Star Wars tickets?

15
00:01:06,066 --> 00:01:09,569
No, it's Steel Magnolias 2: Even Steelier.

16
00:01:11,113 --> 00:01:12,405
The website's frozen. I can't get in!

17
00:01:12,572 --> 00:01:13,573
-LEONARD: Yeah, me, too.
-Same here.

18
00:01:13,740 --> 00:01:15,825
-Guys, they're gonna sell out!
-What are we gonna do?

19
00:01:15,992 --> 00:01:17,952
All right, this goes
against everything I stand for,

20
00:01:18,120 --> 00:01:19,996
but desperate times
call for desperate measures.

21
00:01:20,163 --> 00:01:21,164
Lord...

22
00:01:24,542 --> 00:01:25,627
This is Sheldon Cooper.

23
00:01:26,711 --> 00:01:28,045
You're good friends with my mom.

24
00:01:29,339 --> 00:01:32,384
I know I've spent my life
denying that you exist.

25
00:01:32,550 --> 00:01:34,594
-Got 'em!
-Yeah, and I will continue to do so!

26
00:01:36,388 --> 00:01:38,431
(THEME SONG PLAYING)

27
00:02:00,453 --> 00:02:01,496
I'm really happy
you and Amy are back together.

28
00:02:01,579 --> 00:02:02,539
PRESENT DAY

29
00:02:02,622 --> 00:02:03,706
Thank you.

30
00:02:03,873 --> 00:02:06,000
I'm also really happy,
but I can't pretend it's for you.

31
00:02:06,168 --> 00:02:07,669
New Star Wars in three days! (CHUCKLES)

32
00:02:09,296 --> 00:02:11,464
Hey, Thursday can't get here soon enough.

33
00:02:11,631 --> 00:02:14,176
I'm taking off work
to watch the original trilogy

34
00:02:14,342 --> 00:02:16,803
while I eat enough Star Wars
cereal to choke a Wookiee.

35
00:02:18,971 --> 00:02:21,641
Uh, sweetie, you do realize
Thursday is Amy's birthday.

36
00:02:21,808 --> 00:02:24,269
Yeah, and you do realize
I bought my ticket

37
00:02:24,436 --> 00:02:25,728
when Amy and I were broken up?

38
00:02:27,564 --> 00:02:29,191
I hope you didn't
need anything in that case,

39
00:02:29,357 --> 00:02:30,358
'cause it's closed.

40
00:02:32,485 --> 00:02:33,653
You guys just got back together.

41
00:02:33,820 --> 00:02:35,613
You might not want
to ditch her on her birthday.

42
00:02:35,780 --> 00:02:37,824
I think Penny has a point.
You can see it another day.

43
00:02:37,990 --> 00:02:39,826
But someone might spoil the movie.

44
00:02:39,992 --> 00:02:42,036
No, no one can spoil
Amy's birthday for me.

45
00:02:42,204 --> 00:02:44,247
Surprise! She's even older.
Who saw that coming?

46
00:02:46,499 --> 00:02:48,418
Aw! That's nice. Put that on her cake.

47
00:02:59,971 --> 00:03:01,180
Oh, great. This again.

48
00:03:03,558 --> 00:03:06,185
Arthur? What brings you back?

49
00:03:06,353 --> 00:03:08,688
Beats me. I just

50
00:03:08,855 --> 00:03:10,982
hope this isn't a sex dream.

51
00:03:13,360 --> 00:03:16,779
In the past, you've come to me
when I'm struggling with a dilemma.

52
00:03:17,154 --> 00:03:20,658
And... And the one time where...
Where you were afraid,

53
00:03:20,825 --> 00:03:23,245
and you needed me for...
For a night light.

54
00:03:26,205 --> 00:03:27,540
What's... What's troubling you?

55
00:03:28,708 --> 00:03:30,543
Well...

56
00:03:30,710 --> 00:03:32,169
My friends are telling me

57
00:03:32,337 --> 00:03:35,172
I shouldn't abandon my girlfriend
on her birthday

58
00:03:35,340 --> 00:03:37,425
to see the new Star Wars movie.

59
00:03:37,675 --> 00:03:39,219
Well, sounds right.

60
00:03:41,221 --> 00:03:44,807
Can... Can I get out of this mumu now?

61
00:03:46,643 --> 00:03:48,478
Those are the robes of the Jedi,

62
00:03:48,645 --> 00:03:51,564
the guardians of peace
and justice in the galaxy.

63
00:03:51,898 --> 00:03:54,734
And they... They...
They don't wear underwear.

64
00:04:00,865 --> 00:04:05,161
So, you agree with my friends
that I should skip the premiere?

65
00:04:06,788 --> 00:04:08,998
Do... Do you love this girl?

66
00:04:09,206 --> 00:04:10,417
Yes.

67
00:04:10,583 --> 00:04:13,920
But she knows
how important Star Wars is to me.

68
00:04:14,170 --> 00:04:16,506
Well, maybe you should show her how...

69
00:04:16,673 --> 00:04:19,091
How important she is to you.

70
00:04:19,759 --> 00:04:21,803
By seeing the movie she'd want me to see?

71
00:04:24,221 --> 00:04:27,058
Sheldon, you can see this movie
whenever you want.

72
00:04:28,435 --> 00:04:31,563
But you only have a limited number of days

73
00:04:31,729 --> 00:04:34,148
that you can be with this woman.

74
00:04:35,232 --> 00:04:36,233
Be with her.

75
00:04:39,111 --> 00:04:40,196
You're right.

76
00:04:40,697 --> 00:04:41,698
Great.

77
00:04:43,325 --> 00:04:44,659
Where are you going?

78
00:04:45,284 --> 00:04:47,287
I don't know,

79
00:04:47,454 --> 00:04:49,414
but, hopefully,
somewhere I can wear pants.

80
00:04:52,584 --> 00:04:53,960
(CELL PHONE RINGING)

81
00:04:59,507 --> 00:05:00,800
Sheldon, what's wrong?

82
00:05:01,217 --> 00:05:04,220
I wanted to let you know
I'll be spending your birthday with you.

83
00:05:05,472 --> 00:05:06,556
Okay.

84
00:05:07,890 --> 00:05:10,685
See, I had tickets
to the Star Wars premiere that night,

85
00:05:10,977 --> 00:05:12,979
but Professor Proton
came to me in a dream,

86
00:05:13,145 --> 00:05:16,023
dressed as Obi-Wan Kenobi,
and convinced me I should be with you.

87
00:05:17,274 --> 00:05:18,275
Obi-what?

88
00:05:19,777 --> 00:05:21,821
I'll let you get back to sleep now.
Good night.

89
00:05:21,988 --> 00:05:24,866
Okay. Good night. Wait... Sheldon,

90
00:05:25,032 --> 00:05:27,619
were you actually not gonna
spend my birthday with me?

91
00:05:30,372 --> 00:05:31,623
(YAWNING) It's late. Got to go. Bye.

92
00:05:33,916 --> 00:05:35,167
Good for Sheldon deciding

93
00:05:35,335 --> 00:05:37,211
-to stay with Amy on her birthday.
-I know.

94
00:05:37,462 --> 00:05:39,130
It's still gonna be weird
to see the movie without him.

95
00:05:39,631 --> 00:05:42,967
Well, we could wait a couple of days
and see it together.

96
00:05:44,176 --> 00:05:45,177
(ALL LAUGHING)

97
00:05:47,263 --> 00:05:48,347
Hello.

98
00:05:48,515 --> 00:05:50,349
Hey. We're going to the comic book store.
You want to come?

99
00:05:50,517 --> 00:05:51,518
No, I can't.

100
00:05:51,684 --> 00:05:53,853
I need to make preparations
for Amy's birthday.

101
00:05:54,186 --> 00:05:56,939
Which leads me
to the following bit of business.

102
00:05:57,106 --> 00:05:59,692
This is my ticket to Star Wars.

103
00:05:59,859 --> 00:06:00,902
I don't have to tell you

104
00:06:01,068 --> 00:06:04,572
it is worth far more
than its face value of $15.50.

105
00:06:06,115 --> 00:06:08,284
I trust you'll give it to someone worthy.

106
00:06:09,076 --> 00:06:10,327
You got it.

107
00:06:10,495 --> 00:06:11,829
Well, Penny might want to join us--

108
00:06:11,996 --> 00:06:14,290
This is my ticket to Star Wars.

109
00:06:15,833 --> 00:06:19,421
-(KNOCKING ON DOOR)
-SHELDON: Penny? Penny? Penny?

110
00:06:19,879 --> 00:06:21,631
What happens if I say, "Come in"?

111
00:06:21,964 --> 00:06:23,299
Well, find out.

112
00:06:23,550 --> 00:06:24,551
Come in!

113
00:06:28,638 --> 00:06:29,639
(KNOCKING ON DOOR)

114
00:06:29,806 --> 00:06:32,434
SHELDON: Bernadette?
Bernadette? Bernadette?

115
00:06:32,684 --> 00:06:33,685
Come in!

116
00:06:35,728 --> 00:06:37,480
Keep it up. I got nowhere else to be.

117
00:06:39,065 --> 00:06:40,066
Just come in.

118
00:06:41,943 --> 00:06:43,778
For future reference,
if I want to watch Mean Girls,

119
00:06:43,945 --> 00:06:45,071
I'll stream it on Netflix.

120
00:06:47,073 --> 00:06:48,575
We're sorry. What do you need?

121
00:06:48,741 --> 00:06:49,742
Well, as you know,

122
00:06:49,909 --> 00:06:51,911
I'll be celebrating
Amy's birthday with her,

123
00:06:52,078 --> 00:06:55,081
and I could use your assistance
in helping me select the perfect gift.

124
00:06:55,247 --> 00:06:56,458
-Sure.
-Well, so far,

125
00:06:56,624 --> 00:06:57,625
I've come up with three ideas.

126
00:06:57,792 --> 00:06:59,210
The first is a chance for her

127
00:06:59,376 --> 00:07:01,420
to play the harp
with the LA Philharmonic.

128
00:07:01,588 --> 00:07:03,214
Wow. You can really arrange that?

129
00:07:03,380 --> 00:07:04,882
Well, I said a chance, you know.

130
00:07:05,049 --> 00:07:07,635
When you tell them it's your birthday
at Bennigan's, they make a fuss.

131
00:07:07,802 --> 00:07:09,512
I don't see why the Philharmonic
would be any different.

132
00:07:11,097 --> 00:07:13,099
How about
something a little more realistic?

133
00:07:13,265 --> 00:07:15,727
Well, Amy enjoys
knitting her own sweaters.

134
00:07:15,893 --> 00:07:18,563
So, I was thinking
of getting her an all-expense-paid trip

135
00:07:18,730 --> 00:07:20,857
to the Wisconsin Sheep &amp; Wool Festival.

136
00:07:24,443 --> 00:07:26,153
Sorry. I was waiting for the "bazinga."

137
00:07:28,030 --> 00:07:29,782
Hold on. It could be romantic.

138
00:07:29,949 --> 00:07:31,075
The two of them away together,

139
00:07:31,242 --> 00:07:33,202
keeping each other warm
in snowy Wisconsin.

140
00:07:33,369 --> 00:07:35,037
No, no, no, no. She'd be going alone.

141
00:07:35,204 --> 00:07:37,624
But if you think I'm afraid of birds,
you should see me around sheep.

142
00:07:38,875 --> 00:07:40,292
Okay, well, what's the third option?

143
00:07:40,460 --> 00:07:41,836
That I have coitus with her.

144
00:07:42,086 --> 00:07:43,087
(GLASS SHATTERS)

145
00:07:50,762 --> 00:07:53,139
What do you think about
giving Sheldon's ticket to Stuart?

146
00:07:53,848 --> 00:07:54,891
I don't know.

147
00:07:55,057 --> 00:07:57,018
Have you ever
seen a movie with Stuart before?

148
00:07:57,184 --> 00:07:58,853
It's like going with your grandpa.

149
00:08:00,187 --> 00:08:01,230
Instead of eating popcorn,

150
00:08:01,397 --> 00:08:03,566
he brings little pieces
of chicken in Tupperware

151
00:08:03,733 --> 00:08:04,859
and a thermos full of soup.

152
00:08:06,778 --> 00:08:07,820
He's not that bad.

153
00:08:08,070 --> 00:08:10,865
Hey, Stuart, got any plans Thursday night?

154
00:08:11,032 --> 00:08:13,535
My... My doctor's worried
about my circulation,

155
00:08:13,701 --> 00:08:15,662
so I was thinking about
walking around the mall.

156
00:08:17,664 --> 00:08:18,831
Why?

157
00:08:18,998 --> 00:08:20,124
-Well--
-Hey, you guys.

158
00:08:20,291 --> 00:08:21,668
Make sure to wear sensible shoes.

159
00:08:21,834 --> 00:08:23,503
Wil, want to go to Star Wars, Thursday?

160
00:08:24,253 --> 00:08:25,337
Absolutely.

161
00:08:25,505 --> 00:08:26,714
Fine. Take Wil.

162
00:08:26,881 --> 00:08:28,716
See if he brings you clam chowder.

163
00:08:31,177 --> 00:08:32,970
Okay, okay, okay. Okay, okay...

164
00:08:33,137 --> 00:08:35,222
Let's... Let's...
Let's just recap our options.

165
00:08:35,389 --> 00:08:38,017
All right, we've got
harp thing, sheep thing...

166
00:08:38,225 --> 00:08:39,268
Wild thang.

167
00:08:42,939 --> 00:08:44,481
Which do you think she'd prefer?

168
00:08:45,482 --> 00:08:48,194
Because I checked
the Sheep and Wool Festival website,

169
00:08:48,360 --> 00:08:49,946
and there's only 8,000 tickets left.

170
00:08:52,198 --> 00:08:55,743
Okay. Sheldon, being physical with Amy
is a huge step for you.

171
00:08:55,910 --> 00:08:57,286
Yeah, are you ready for this?

172
00:08:57,870 --> 00:09:00,915
Intimacy in any form
has been challenging for me,

173
00:09:01,082 --> 00:09:03,334
but I'd like to show her
how important she is,

174
00:09:03,500 --> 00:09:05,878
and it feels like
now might be the right time.

175
00:09:06,128 --> 00:09:07,797
Sheldon, that's so beautiful.

176
00:09:08,255 --> 00:09:09,465
Then it's settled.

177
00:09:09,632 --> 00:09:11,718
Amy's birthday present
will be my genitals.

178
00:09:17,557 --> 00:09:18,808
Thanks for taking me out.

179
00:09:18,975 --> 00:09:20,517
Well, you're spending
your birthday with Sheldon.

180
00:09:20,685 --> 00:09:21,894
Why not celebrate early?

181
00:09:22,061 --> 00:09:23,062
So, where do you want to go?

182
00:09:23,229 --> 00:09:25,857
I heard that new Mexican place
on Greene Street is good.

183
00:09:26,023 --> 00:09:27,399
Sure, sure.

184
00:09:27,567 --> 00:09:29,902
Or we could take you to get a bikini wax.

185
00:09:33,072 --> 00:09:35,700
Why would I get a bikini wax
for my birthday?

186
00:09:35,950 --> 00:09:38,285
(STAMMERS) I don't know.
It was just a thought.

187
00:09:38,452 --> 00:09:39,996
I think I'll just stick to Mexican.

188
00:09:40,997 --> 00:09:41,998
Great.

189
00:09:42,164 --> 00:09:44,792
And then, maybe after,
we can watch a dirty movie,

190
00:09:44,959 --> 00:09:47,378
and if anybody has any questions
about what happened or how,

191
00:09:47,544 --> 00:09:48,630
we can answer them.

192
00:09:51,340 --> 00:09:53,259
Okay, what is going on?

193
00:09:53,425 --> 00:09:54,593
We just want you to be prepared

194
00:09:54,761 --> 00:09:57,429
for any surprises
that might happen tomorrow.

195
00:09:57,597 --> 00:09:59,265
What surprises?

196
00:09:59,515 --> 00:10:00,516
(EXHALES)

197
00:10:01,809 --> 00:10:04,771
We don't want to spoil anything,

198
00:10:04,937 --> 00:10:08,149
but you should know that
Sheldon said he's ready to be physical.

199
00:10:08,315 --> 00:10:10,234
You shut your damn mouth!

200
00:10:14,947 --> 00:10:17,033
You actually heard him say this?

201
00:10:17,199 --> 00:10:19,952
Yes. He said he wants to do something
to show you how much you mean to him.

202
00:10:20,161 --> 00:10:21,162
(EXHALES)

203
00:10:21,453 --> 00:10:24,206
I... I can't believe it. I...

204
00:10:26,083 --> 00:10:28,085
I don't know what to say.

205
00:10:28,670 --> 00:10:31,673
Well, we're really happy for you,
and we know how much he cares--

206
00:10:31,839 --> 00:10:33,299
I do know what to say! Let's get me waxed!

207
00:10:43,434 --> 00:10:46,062
Why isn't it ever
Angie Dickinson's bedroom?

208
00:10:49,356 --> 00:10:50,357
You're back.

209
00:10:50,607 --> 00:10:53,444
It... It doesn't seem like it's up to me.

210
00:10:54,987 --> 00:10:57,364
I suppose you're here

211
00:10:57,531 --> 00:11:00,326
because I've decided
to be physical with my girlfriend,

212
00:11:00,492 --> 00:11:02,704
and I've never done that before.

213
00:11:03,830 --> 00:11:06,415
Excuse me for a moment.

214
00:11:12,922 --> 00:11:14,506
(LIGHTSABER ACTIVATING)

215
00:11:23,975 --> 00:11:25,226
Well, it was worth a shot.

216
00:11:27,729 --> 00:11:30,106
So, can you help me?

217
00:11:31,315 --> 00:11:32,775
Uh, all right, um...

218
00:11:33,901 --> 00:11:36,528
Once... Once the man gets

219
00:11:36,695 --> 00:11:39,656
the woman out of her...
Out of her bloomers...

220
00:11:40,074 --> 00:11:42,368
No. Not that.

221
00:11:42,534 --> 00:11:44,703
I... I understand the mechanics.

222
00:11:44,871 --> 00:11:47,456
Oh, good. Good. 'Cause

223
00:11:47,623 --> 00:11:51,252
I have no idea what kids these days

224
00:11:51,543 --> 00:11:53,755
are calling their... Their parts.

225
00:11:56,715 --> 00:11:58,384
I think they say "junk."

226
00:12:00,427 --> 00:12:02,263
What is happening to this world?

227
00:12:05,349 --> 00:12:08,477
What... What do you
actually need to know?

228
00:12:10,312 --> 00:12:13,315
This is an important night for us,

229
00:12:13,482 --> 00:12:17,194
and I'm worried I might be overwhelmed
and ruin everything.

230
00:12:18,154 --> 00:12:22,533
(SIGHS) Sheldon,
if you're with the right person,

231
00:12:22,699 --> 00:12:24,701
it'll be okay.

232
00:12:26,412 --> 00:12:27,413
(CHUCKLES SOFTLY)

233
00:12:27,704 --> 00:12:29,623
Thank you, Arthur.

234
00:12:29,957 --> 00:12:32,709
You are the wisest of the wise.

235
00:12:33,627 --> 00:12:35,546
Well, that's...
That's very nice of you to say,

236
00:12:35,712 --> 00:12:38,382
but I think I'm just an expression of...

237
00:12:38,757 --> 00:12:41,052
Of your unconscious mind.

238
00:12:41,302 --> 00:12:43,637
Oh, sure.

239
00:12:43,805 --> 00:12:46,515
Well, you're fun to look at.

240
00:12:51,645 --> 00:12:52,646
Tonight's the night!

241
00:12:52,814 --> 00:12:54,481
Yeah, the wait is finally over!

242
00:12:54,648 --> 00:12:57,109
I know.
Then you'll finally stop talking about it!

243
00:12:58,444 --> 00:12:59,736
-Ready to go?
-Let's do this.

244
00:13:00,029 --> 00:13:01,655
-Have fun, guys!
-We will.

245
00:13:01,823 --> 00:13:03,950
-I can't believe Sheldon gave this up.
-I know.

246
00:13:04,116 --> 00:13:05,784
We're gonna have
so much more fun than him.

247
00:13:08,955 --> 00:13:09,956
No, they're not.

248
00:13:12,166 --> 00:13:14,001
Knowing them, they will.

249
00:13:15,878 --> 00:13:17,254
(INDISTINCT CHATTER)

250
00:13:19,215 --> 00:13:21,217
-T-minus 15 minutes!
-(ALL CHUCKLING)

251
00:13:21,633 --> 00:13:23,510
-Oh, did you hear from Wil?
-Yeah, he's on his way.

252
00:13:23,928 --> 00:13:24,971
Time for bladder check.

253
00:13:25,471 --> 00:13:26,472
Check.

254
00:13:26,889 --> 00:13:28,640
-Check.
-Check.

255
00:13:28,807 --> 00:13:29,976
Wait.

256
00:13:31,477 --> 00:13:32,603
Screw it. I'm holding it.

257
00:13:33,395 --> 00:13:34,771
(PEOPLE BOOING)

258
00:13:35,022 --> 00:13:36,440
What is everyone booing at?

259
00:13:43,322 --> 00:13:44,406
Hey, guys. What's up?

260
00:13:45,950 --> 00:13:47,994
Uh... Hey, Wil. What you doin'?

261
00:13:48,494 --> 00:13:50,662
I was on Star Trek.
Just rooting for the home team.

262
00:13:51,830 --> 00:13:52,915
MAN: Star Trek stinks!

263
00:13:53,207 --> 00:13:54,959
Yeah? Live long and suck it!

264
00:14:02,841 --> 00:14:03,842
(KNOCKING ON DOOR)

265
00:14:04,010 --> 00:14:07,304
SHELDON: Birthday girl?
Birthday girl? Birthday girl?

266
00:14:10,975 --> 00:14:11,976
Come in!

267
00:14:12,684 --> 00:14:13,685
Oh!

268
00:14:19,984 --> 00:14:21,193
-Hi, Sheldon.
-Hello.

269
00:14:21,360 --> 00:14:22,403
Sorry I'm late.

270
00:14:22,569 --> 00:14:24,321
I also got you a balloon,

271
00:14:24,488 --> 00:14:26,282
but it floated away,
and I chased it for a while.

272
00:14:27,741 --> 00:14:29,201
That's okay. Come on in.

273
00:14:29,618 --> 00:14:30,619
Thank you.

274
00:14:31,412 --> 00:14:33,414
Um, I'll just... I'm gonna go
put these in water.

275
00:14:33,580 --> 00:14:34,916
Okay.

276
00:14:36,042 --> 00:14:37,584
Oh! This is different.

277
00:14:37,919 --> 00:14:39,878
Hmm. Candles and music.

278
00:14:40,046 --> 00:14:41,047
Do you like it?

279
00:14:41,213 --> 00:14:42,256
It's kind of spooky.

280
00:14:43,882 --> 00:14:44,967
I can change it back.

281
00:14:45,134 --> 00:14:46,635
No, no, no. It's your birthday.

282
00:14:46,802 --> 00:14:49,763
And as long as no one jumps out
in a hockey mask, I'll be fine.

283
00:14:53,350 --> 00:14:54,476
(CHUCKLES SOFTLY)

284
00:14:55,144 --> 00:14:56,270
So...

285
00:14:58,230 --> 00:14:59,856
What'd you have in mind for tonight?

286
00:15:00,232 --> 00:15:03,069
I thought I could take you out
to a nice birthday dinner.

287
00:15:03,235 --> 00:15:06,238
Now, if we pick a place east of here,
we might find the balloon.

288
00:15:07,949 --> 00:15:11,077
Um, that sounds nice,

289
00:15:11,243 --> 00:15:13,829
but I'm not really hungry right now.

290
00:15:13,996 --> 00:15:15,957
I thought, maybe,

291
00:15:16,582 --> 00:15:19,376
-we could do presents first.
-Oh!

292
00:15:21,420 --> 00:15:23,047
All right. Um...

293
00:15:25,049 --> 00:15:27,926
I should probably tell you
something about this gift.

294
00:15:28,594 --> 00:15:31,472
You mean, before you...

295
00:15:33,224 --> 00:15:34,225
Give it to me?

296
00:15:38,104 --> 00:15:39,188
Yes.

297
00:15:40,272 --> 00:15:43,275
May I ask you a question before I...

298
00:15:44,026 --> 00:15:45,027
Give it to you?

299
00:15:47,529 --> 00:15:48,990
-Of course.
-Why are we saying

300
00:15:49,156 --> 00:15:51,617
"give it to you" like that?

301
00:15:52,451 --> 00:15:54,453
Sheldon,

302
00:15:55,246 --> 00:15:57,957
I know your present is

303
00:15:58,457 --> 00:16:00,917
for us to be intimate tonight.

304
00:16:02,003 --> 00:16:03,670
I see.

305
00:16:04,921 --> 00:16:05,922
Is that all right?

306
00:16:12,138 --> 00:16:13,805
I'm sorry,
but this is a litigious society.

307
00:16:13,973 --> 00:16:15,141
I'm gonna need verbal consent.

308
00:16:18,978 --> 00:16:20,062
Yes.

309
00:16:22,189 --> 00:16:24,233
You know what, let me
pull a quick contract off the Internet--

310
00:16:30,656 --> 00:16:32,992
So, if you don't like Star Wars,
why are you here?

311
00:16:33,200 --> 00:16:34,368
Oh, I'm just having fun.

312
00:16:34,535 --> 00:16:36,120
Everyone takes Star Wars so seriously.

313
00:16:36,287 --> 00:16:38,789
Like if the movie's bad,
it's gonna ruin their lives.

314
00:16:38,955 --> 00:16:40,624
Is it bad? Did you hear something?

315
00:16:41,208 --> 00:16:43,294
Oh, my God. It's bad. Somebody kill me.

316
00:16:44,795 --> 00:16:46,422
See? That's what I mean.

317
00:16:46,588 --> 00:16:47,589
When you wake up in the morning,

318
00:16:47,756 --> 00:16:50,342
whether this is the greatest movie ever
or a total piece of crap,

319
00:16:50,509 --> 00:16:51,968
your life isn't gonna change at all.

320
00:16:54,055 --> 00:16:55,097
He's right.

321
00:16:55,264 --> 00:16:56,265
Yeah.

322
00:16:57,224 --> 00:16:58,267
No matter what happens,

323
00:16:58,434 --> 00:16:59,851
we're coming back tomorrow
to watch it again.

324
00:17:03,189 --> 00:17:05,357
Do you think Sheldon's actually
gonna go through with it?

325
00:17:05,524 --> 00:17:07,776
I don't know. He said he's ready.

326
00:17:07,943 --> 00:17:09,361
Yeah, but he also swore this was the year

327
00:17:09,528 --> 00:17:11,530
he'd be able to
pull the guts out of a pumpkin.

328
00:17:13,490 --> 00:17:14,741
Yeah, well, I'm gonna stay positive.

329
00:17:14,908 --> 00:17:16,618
I mean, we talked.
I told him what women like.

330
00:17:16,785 --> 00:17:19,205
And after he stopped giggling,
he seemed pretty sure of himself.

331
00:17:33,302 --> 00:17:34,345
(CHUCKLES) Hi.

332
00:17:35,221 --> 00:17:36,388
Hello.

333
00:17:38,182 --> 00:17:40,059
So, um...

334
00:17:42,144 --> 00:17:43,687
Should I get under the covers with you?

335
00:17:45,606 --> 00:17:46,815
All right.

336
00:18:08,087 --> 00:18:09,213
-Hello--
-Hi!

337
00:18:13,134 --> 00:18:15,094
Why are you shaking? Are you cold?

338
00:18:15,969 --> 00:18:18,597
I'm just... (EXHALES) Really nervous.

339
00:18:19,014 --> 00:18:20,015
Why?

340
00:18:21,142 --> 00:18:23,018
Well,

341
00:18:23,394 --> 00:18:25,604
I've been waiting for this for so long,

342
00:18:26,605 --> 00:18:28,774
I've just built it up in my head.

343
00:18:29,608 --> 00:18:31,777
I don't know what to expect.

344
00:18:32,444 --> 00:18:34,405
Neither do I.

345
00:18:35,281 --> 00:18:38,992
But, we can find out together.

346
00:18:41,995 --> 00:18:43,205
Okay.

347
00:18:51,172 --> 00:18:52,298
I'm really nervous.

348
00:18:54,633 --> 00:18:55,634
I know.

349
00:18:55,967 --> 00:18:57,761
We've been waiting so long for this.

350
00:18:59,638 --> 00:19:02,098
And we've built it up
in our heads so much.

351
00:19:03,684 --> 00:19:05,769
Guys, it's just a movie.

352
00:19:06,478 --> 00:19:07,479
-That's true.
-He's right.

353
00:19:07,646 --> 00:19:08,772
-It is.
-(CHUCKLES)

354
00:19:09,231 --> 00:19:11,858
Although, we all remember Jar Jar.

355
00:19:13,819 --> 00:19:16,197
Leonard, I'm scared again.

356
00:19:19,074 --> 00:19:21,452
A FEW HOURS LATER,
IN A BEDROOM NOT FAR AWAY....

357
00:19:22,661 --> 00:19:25,331
Well, I enjoyed that
more than I thought I would.

358
00:19:33,630 --> 00:19:34,715
Me, too.

359
00:19:37,509 --> 00:19:40,554
I look forward to your next
birthday when we do it again.

360
00:19:43,515 --> 00:19:44,850
That works for me!

361
00:19:46,227 --> 00:19:48,187
I enjoyed that
more than I thought I would.

362
00:19:52,483 --> 00:19:54,401
I don't think I can walk right now.

363
00:19:59,948 --> 00:20:01,032
ARTHUR: Sheldon?

364
00:20:02,117 --> 00:20:03,369
Sheldon.

365
00:20:03,869 --> 00:20:04,870
Arthur.

366
00:20:05,036 --> 00:20:06,372
What are you doing here?

367
00:20:06,538 --> 00:20:09,541
I... I... I don't think
I need any more advice.

368
00:20:09,875 --> 00:20:11,293
I... I was just curious.

369
00:20:14,838 --> 00:20:16,215
How did it go?

370
00:20:21,887 --> 00:20:23,013
It was amazing.

371
00:20:24,014 --> 00:20:25,557
I... I saw it a few days later.

372
00:20:25,724 --> 00:20:26,808
What a movie.

373
00:20:32,939 --> 00:20:34,900
But, what... What about Amy?

374
00:20:35,150 --> 00:20:36,360
Oh! Uh...

375
00:20:36,568 --> 00:20:38,028
She liked it fine.

376
00:20:38,194 --> 00:20:41,156
Yeah, but she doesn't have the history
with the franchise I do.

377
00:20:43,742 --> 00:20:44,868
Okay.

378
00:20:46,412 --> 00:20:47,579
Good... Good talk.

